      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is double the usual maximum adult dose:\n- **Immediate-release:** 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** 2,000 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check what was intended. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day:** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose:** if you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me what it is.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd suggest you verify it with pharmacy first."
      }
