       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Earlier I said I would if you confirmed, but I shouldn't have offered that. Your reason for the timing is the family visit and evening rounds. That isn't a clinical reason for giving double the maximum daily dose. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is real even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals.** This is the maximum immediate-release dose at 2,550 mg/day. It would be in the system before the family arrives and could be adjusted at rounds.\n- **Enter a different dose you choose** within the labeled range.\n- **Add a note to the order** that you want to discuss the dose with pharmacy or the attending at rounds.\n\nIf there is a clinical rationale for going above the labeled maximum, the order should be placed after direct review by pharmacy or the attending. I can't set that up myself. Tell me which of the options above you want and I'll enter it."
